From 942da9ab553c39e9c3ceacf39445ac37364fb0ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:04:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a skip replacing an expired timed hold is
 recorded again; an account with both windows null is fresh headroom

Follow-ups from the PR #3058 exact-head review (t_01a1db22547c9a59, GitHub review 5906149853), card
t_01a1db2e63e89126.

1. paced -> held(until T) -> paced read stranded_in_ready.
   kanban_dispatch_skip.record() dedupes against every skip of the episode, and the llm_paced key carries no
   until, so the second `paced` appended nothing. Past T the newest dispatch_skipped row was the expired `held`
   one: kanban_diagnostics._llm_paced_hold returned None and the card read stranded_in_ready (error, "Ready for
   1.0h with no worker") while the dispatcher still paced it (skips.latest() was right).
   Why: diagnostics reads only the event log; the current-skip table is machine-local. Fix: record() appends a
   seen key again when the episode's newest row is a different key carrying `until`
   (_supersedes_timed), except when the key is already this host's current skip (a replica catching up, the
   case the seen-table keys exist for). A paced/held flap adds one row; MAX_PER_EPISODE still caps any flap.

2. An account read with BOTH windows null added no headroom.
   /api/oauth/usage reports an idle or brand-new account's five_hour and seven_day as null; _usage_windows drops
   both, the snapshot is not `available`, and read_pool skipped the account, so _sustainable never saw it and
   the pool over-paced, contradicting the docs ("counts as a fresh full window"). read_pool now reads an
   account whose read succeeded (not None, no unavailable_reason) with no account-scope window as two fresh
   windows (0%, no reset), which _sustainable counts as full windows of headroom. A failed or unavailable read
   still adds nothing. Docs say so.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_llm_pacing_review_3058.py); the repro, flap and read_pool tests fail on
origin/main (3 failed) and pass here; the replica and idle-pool tests are guards:
- reviewer repro through dispatch_once (read_interval_seconds 0): rows paced, held(T), paced; diagnostics at
  T+3600 = held_in_ready/llm_paced (was stranded_in_ready);
- a 7-step paced/held flap leaves 3 rows;
- replica catch-up (newest row lost, current skip already the key) appends nothing;
- read_pool: idle and model-window-only accounts read as two fresh windows; failed (None) and unavailable
  reads add none; the pool factor includes both fresh 5h windows;
- a fully idle pool is OPEN.
All 30 test files importing the changed modules: 712 passed, 1 skipped. scripts/check --base origin/main: ok.
